# Auto-Fix Execution Boundaries

The fix agent must not independently reclassify findings.

Fix eligibility is determined by:

```text
.review/rpa-fix-readiness.md

The fix agent should only apply findings explicitly classified as:

Auto-fixable

Do not apply:

Semi-auto-fixable findings
Manual-only findings
Findings without fix-readiness classification
Execution Rule

For each Auto-fixable finding:

Locate the affected file/workflow/activity.
Verify the finding evidence still matches the current repository state.
Apply the smallest safe patch.
Avoid unrelated formatting or structural changes.
Record the applied fix in .review/rpa-fix-result.md.

If the evidence does not match:

skip the fix
record the reason
Safety Brake

Even if a finding is marked Auto-fixable, skip it if the actual edit would change:

Business Logic
Queue Semantics
Retry Behavior
Transaction Lifecycle
Reporting Lifecycle
Framework-Owned Behavior
Exception Routing
External System Behavior
Credential Lifecycle

Document skipped items clearly.

Allowed Execution Style

Prefer:

Minimal Patches
Localized Edits
Deterministic Changes
Reviewable Diffs

Avoid:

Broad Refactors
Opportunistic Cleanup
Unrequested Improvements
Multi-file Semantic Changes
Output Requirement

After applying fixes, write:

.review/rpa-fix-result.md

The result must include:

Applied Fixes
Skipped Auto-Fixable Findings
Modified Files
Validation Notes
Remaining Risks